            rl-row("R47", "switches", "measure", "FORM_DS4_SUBMIT_EVERY (default 2): the one DS4 switch with no cited evidence; an A/B at 1/2/4 on the real blob settles it", "open", "a first measurement run was in flight when its process ended 2026-09-03; worktree gone, nothing recovered; owed as a bounded run after the doc wave"),
            rl-row("R48", "switches", "wire-or-drop", "DEFAULT_TOKEN_BYTES / METAL_BANDWIDTH_BYTES_PER_MS / TOKEN_SWAP_CELL: three Form-computed, receipt-cited values ask-ds4.fk exports into the environment that nothing downstream ever reads -- either wire a real consumer or stop exporting them", "released", "78f2b2d6: all three were the losing half of a real 2026-08-13/08-19 architectural fork (the admission math moved onto the Form side, the carrier exports were never deleted); dropped, values wired into a real footer line instead"),
            rl-row("R51", "seed", "lower", "fk_walk_cold (~1,770 lines, 11% of the seed, pure tag dispatch) lowers into grammars/form-eval.fk's fef-optable rows -- the reducer IS Form (stone S3b, in flight since 2026-06-29); C keeps a thin trampoline until form-eval runs the body at speed", "open", "proof: form-eval-band, form-eval-full-band, native-vs-rented 11111 bit-identical through the Form reducer; measure: seed lines"),
            rl-row("R52", "seed", "lower", "the source runner (fk_src_*, ~2,100 lines) lowers into source-compiler.fk's lane; C keeps only mmap and exec of the .fkb/.dylib image", "open", "proof: every band in form/fourth-arm-bands.txt runs through the Form runner; freshness band 31"),
            rl-row("R53", "seed", "lower", "the .fkb loader/writer (~640 lines) lowers into fkc-table-serialize.fk / runtime-program-image-fkb-micro-walker.fk, which already describe the format", "open", "proof: program-image-fkb bands; a .fkb written by Form loads in C and vice versa, byte-identical"),
            rl-row("R54", "seed", "lower", "the --src parser and fk_sparse (~1,330 lines) lower into form-parse.fk / the BMF cursor (stone S3b seed-drop): source enters through the cursor, the C parser becomes the one-time bootstrap it already calls itself", "open", "proof: ground quartet through the cursor; 4+-arg ops lowered natively (closes R19's named gap)"),
